codex
The diagnostic found the actual Blender-state bug: the imported GLB arrived with all mesh elements selected, so “separate selected hair faces” separated the entire mesh and left the skin object empty. I’m explicitly clearing edit-mode selection before applying the classified face mask. That explains every zero-intersection result and is now fixed at the source.
apply patch
