codex
The final build audit now shows a genuine cut: 258 faces intersected, 258 boundary edges and 299 on-plane vertices at z = 2.605 m; the capped neck bridge adds 64 planar faces. Hair retains identical z-min/z-max, with only 232 sub-15 mm disconnected fragments removed under the explicit rule. I’m moving into native numeric validation now; material export survivability and the gorget-report wording remain under review before I call the iteration complete.
